    radius - inset

That red placement is wrong for the desired look.

Required Shield look

The Shield should read as a living black protective bubble related visually to the Void:

* Keep the subtle translucent black interior behind the fighter.
* Keep the main black wavy rim in front of the fighter.
* Keep the same red family used by the Void (EDGE_RED).
* Make the perimeter animation visibly wavy in normal gameplay rather than almost imperceptible.
* The shape should continuously and smoothly drift/waver; it must NOT pulse uniformly in and out.
* It should not look spiky, noisy, or jittery.
* Preserve the circle’s overall size and its centering around the character.
* Preserve reduced-motion behavior: reduced-motion still shows the organic irregular shape but freezes its animation.

Increase the Shield wave amplitude enough to make the movement clearly readable. A target around 0.09–0.11 of radius is appropriate instead of the current 0.045, but tune visually if necessary. Keep the slow multi-sine organic approach already used rather than randomizing points per frame.

Red outline placement

The thin red accent must be on the OUTSIDE edge of the black Shield rim.

The current code offsets it inward:

radius - inset

Change the geometry so the red accent occupies the outer half of the black perimeter instead. Conceptually this should become the equivalent of:

radius + inset

where inset is still derived from the black rim width and red accent width.

The final layering should visually read from inside to outside as:

fighter/interior → black Shield boundary → thin red outer edge

The red must not appear as an inner ring around the fighter.

Do not create a second unrelated Shield shape. Both black and red strokes must follow the exact same animated organic wave so they remain locked together.

Update comments in shield-fx.js that currently explicitly describe the red line as being on the “inner side”.

Shield constraints

